\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah Ends Flat On Profit-Taking On Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 1999\par 11:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed flat against the dollar in range-bound dealings Thursday as profit-taking against the U.S. unit saved the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its earlier losses. \par \par \uc2  After trading between 8,750 rupiah (IDR) and IDR8,990, the dollar closed at IDR8,775 in the spot market, unchanged from its close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Offshore participants sold back their dollars after Bank Indonesia checked the exchange rate," said a dealer with a local bank. "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move protected the rupiah against the spill-over of the yen's slide against the dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 1026 GMT (5:26 a.m. EST), the dollar was trading at Y119.73, compared with Y118.90 in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants see the dollar trading between IDR8,600 and IDR9,000 Friday. The weekend mood is expected to leave trading thin and quiet. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has so far ignored the government's plan to close around 40 banks on Feb. 27. \par \par \uc2  The government, however, drove money market rates up as banks prefer to place their money at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than lend to other banks, on fears that the borrowers could be shut down. Small banks bid the overnight rupiah at 60%, but they didn't succeed in attracting funds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana; (62-21) 350 0145; imsentana@ap.org \par \par 