\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals mostly firmer with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 1999\par 02:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0100 GMT - The regionals \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally firmer \par \par \uc2  alongside the yen with trading quiet due to the holiday in \par \par \uc2  Japan today and the forthcoming Chinese New Year holiday for \par \par \uc2  the rest of Asia. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was a little lower ahead of Friday's BOJ policy \par \par \uc2  meeting after U.S. Treasury Secretary Rubin's comment that \par \par \uc2  monetary policy remains a key tool for Japan. \par \par \uc2      But few expect any shift in stance at Friday's meeting. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan is on holiday today for the start of its nine-day \par \par \uc2  Chinese New Year break but the local dollar was trading in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was a little easier after Wednesday's rise \par \par \uc2  on hopes of a fresh disbursement of IMF cash next month and \par \par \uc2  talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is said to be acting through state back to \par \par \uc2  lend some support. \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht was firmer with all eyes on the stock \par \par \uc2  market ahead of corporate results which will begin to trickle \par \par \uc2  out in the next few days. \par \par \uc2      Thailand has passed a streamlined foreclosure law to help \par \par \uc2  speed up the liquidation of companies put out of business by \par \par \uc2  economic crisis. \par \par \uc2      The government sees the new foreclosure bill as essential \par \par \uc2  for nudging bank creditors and troubled debtors to negotiate \par \par \uc2  amicable debt restructuring before the impact of the Thai \par \par \uc2  economic recession deepens. \par \par \uc2  But opposition politicians have voiced objections to one \par \par \uc2  stipulation in the bill that future court foreclosure rulings \par \par \uc2  are final, leaving no legal recourse for debtors to appeal \par \par \uc2  against decisions. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso gave up some of yesterday's late rally which \par \par \uc2  came as a result of large corporate inflows. \par \par \uc2      San Miguel Corp was said to be selling dollar heavily. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won was also a little easier with the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar a touch firmer. \par \par \uc2   Change on the day THU 11 0102GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8580.00......8550.00.........-0.35% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.94........37.00..........0.16% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.00........38.98.........-0.05% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6905.......1.6936..........0.18% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.290.......32.260.........-0.09% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1177.00......1176.40.........-0.05% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....114.20.......115.11..........0.80% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8580.00......2432.00........-71.66% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.95........25.90........-29.91% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.00........26.50........-32.05% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6905.......1.4300........-15.41% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.2900......27.7500........-14.06% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1177.00.......842.00........-28.46% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....114.20......