\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah clambers upwards, progress slow. \b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1999\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah struggled higher against the dollar on Tuesday but trade was particularly thin and uncertainty about the future still hung over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said a weaker dollar yen and improving confidence in the domestic political situation had helped lift the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to stay between 8,600 and 9,000 to the dollar over the week, possibly edging towards the firmer end of the range if students continued to hold off on fresh mass protests against the government, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  By 1000 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 8,800/8,900 to the dollar, unchanged from its morning levels and firmer than the 8,875/8,925 quoted late on Monday in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "The market is quiet, but quiet is good for the rupiah," said one dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta. "There is still a lot of uncertainty, but for the moment Jakarta is quiet and that will help the rupiah." \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said interest rates were likely to remain steady despite the strengthening in the rupiah in recent days. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the interest rate level would be cut now that the rupiah had strengthened through 9,000 to the dollar, Syahril Sabirin said: "I think we will maintain it. For the time being this is reasonable." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its next auction of one-month paper on Wednesday. Last week, the auction yielded a weighted average interest rate of 36.53 percent, up from 35.89 percent the previous week. \par \par \uc2  Year-on-year inflation fell to 70.66 percent in January from 77.63 percent in December, data from the Central Bureau of Statistics (BPS) showed. \par \par \uc2  The BPS said January month-on-month inflation was 2.97 percent, the highest since September, when prices rose 3.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  It said Indonesia's trade surplus rose to $1.61 billion in November from $1.38 billion the previous months. November exports were $3.90 billion, up from $3.77 billion the month before, while imports fell to $2.29 billion from $2.4 billion. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the impact of concerns over the financial stability of Brazil and China, which knocked the rupiah in recent weeks, had also largely faded. \par \par \uc2  An agreement reached last week on new political laws to pave the way for parliamentary elections on June 7 has soothed the market, dealers say. Some had feared failure to agree would mean the elections would be postponed, sparking fresh violence. \par \par \uc2  But the election campaign is widely expected to be violent, and this is keeping many foreign investors out of the country, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Home Affairs Minister Syarwan Hamid was quoted as saying political parties would be banned from taking to the streets and holding mass outdoor rallies during the election campaign, which has been set for May 18 to June 6. \par \par \uc2  "Political parties will not be allowed to mobilise the masses in open fields and party supporters will be barred from taking to the streets," the Jakarta Post newspaper quoted him as saying. \par \par \uc2  "These measures are meant to prevent clashes and violence like in the past." \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week it would continue with "small \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to try to lift the rupiah to 8,000 to the dollar. Indonesia's 1999/2000 budget forecasts an average exchange rate of 7,500 to the dollar. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv22056zd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
