\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals little changed, rupiah firms. \b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1999\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended little changed \par \par \uc2  on Friday with the firmer dollar putting on the pressure, but \par \par \uc2  the rupiah managed to claw back some of its recent losses. \par \par \uc2      The dollar firmed amid optimism about the outlook for the \par \par \uc2  U.S. economy and pessimism about the prospects for European and \par \par \uc2  Japanese growth. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was a rare bright spot in very thin trade \par \par \uc2  and managed to get back the right side of 9,000. \par \par \uc2      Calm on the streets of the capital Jakarta and the \par \par \uc2  expectation that Bank Indonesia will come in and try to give \par \par \uc2  the rupiah's upward momentum a boost kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firm. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said the rupiah's \par \par \uc2  weakness was temporary and "small" amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  support it were continuing. \par \par \uc2      Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the rupiah \par \par \uc2  market today. \par \par \uc2      The market was relieved by the parliament's approval of \par \par \uc2  sweeping political reforms on Thursday, clearing the way for \par \par \uc2  the June elections. \par \par \uc2      The new laws include a reduction in the number of \par \par \uc2  parliamentary seats reserved for the military to 38 from 75, an \par \par \uc2  end to restrictions allowing only three political parties and a \par \par \uc2  proportional representation system for voting. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's top economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita \par \par \uc2  told Reuters Television on Thursday independence for the \par \par \uc2  disputed territory of East Timor could come as early as next \par \par \uc2  year if parliament approved it. \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht was steady but traders are still \par \par \uc2  targeting a drop to the wrong side of 37 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Thailand cut its bank rate to 7.0 percent from \par \par \uc2  12.5 percent effective February 1. \par \par \uc2      The bank rate is that at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  charges on \par \par \uc2  its short-terms loans to private financial institutions. \par \par \uc2      It was the first change in the rate since July 2, 1997, \par \par \uc2  when the baht was devalued and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the rate \par \par \uc2  to 12.5 percent from 10.5 percent. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's November \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account surplus was $1.12 \par \par \uc2  billion with the trade surplus at $1.02 billion. \par \par \uc2      Reserves as at January 22 totalled $29.4 billion against \par \par \uc2  $29.6 on January 15 and $29.8 on January 8. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won was barely changed with state run \par \par \uc2  Export-Import Bank of Korea (Exim) soaking up dollar supplies \par \par \uc2  from exporters and foreign stock funds. \par \par \uc2      Exim Bank officials denied market talk that is was acting \par \par \uc2  on behalf of authorities. \par \par \uc2      "We bought dollars to meet our needs," an Exim official \par \par \uc2  said. "We didn't even buy very much dollars today". \par \par \uc2      He said the bank was preparing for dollars to convert 500 \par \par \uc2  billion won raised through issuing bonds. Exim bank planned to \par \par \uc2  issue the won-denominated bonds soon to help finance domestic \par \par \uc2  exporters. \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso was steady and ignored GDP data for \par \par \uc2  last year. \par \par \uc2      The country's 1998 gross domestic product was down 0.5 \par \par \uc2  percent on the previous full year due to the combined effects \par \par \uc2  of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis and the El Nino phenomenon. \par \par \uc2      The economy last registered negative full-year GDP growth \par \par \uc2  in 1991 after a series of natural disasters. \par \par \uc2      Quarterly data showed a hefty decline in the economy \par \par \uc2  through the course of last year: GDP contracted 1.9 percent \par \par \uc2  between the fourth quarters of 1997 and 1998. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day FRI 29 0935GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8950.00......9200.00.........2.79% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.83........36.83.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.50........38.50.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6905.......1.6895........-0.06% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.290.......32.280........-0.03% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1174.00......1174.30.........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....116.33.......115.32........-0.87% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8950.00......2432.00........-72.83% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.83........25.90........-29.68% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.50........26.50........-31.17% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6905......