\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah advances, mounts attack on 9,000/dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1999\par 03:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 29 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah advanced in early trade on Friday and mounted an assault on 9,000 to the dollar, spurred by dollar selling in the forward market in Singapore and improved confidence in domestic political stability. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded as high as 9,000 to the dollar and was quoted at 8,900/9,000 at 0230 GMT, although dealers said no trades had been done at firmer levels than 9,000. \par \par \uc2  "Some people think 9,000 will hold but that doesn't look likely now," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "There has been relief that the capital has been quiet, we had all expected more trouble this week. So that has changed the outlook of some people in the market and people are selling one-year (dollars) outright in Singapore." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had seen no early signs of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But they said the bank - which did not attempt to stand in the way of the downward trend earlier in the week despite pledges by the governor to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - was likely to step up the amount of dollars it was selling to boost the rupiah's bounce. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  know they can't stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling when that's the way the market is pushing it, but this is their chance to help jack it up," one dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia Governor Syahril Sabirin said on Thursday the rupiah's recent weakening was temporary and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was continuing. \par \par \uc2  "This is temporary," Sabirin told reporters when asked about this week's weakening of the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "Small \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is continuing." \par \par \uc2  Sabirin said earlier this week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would try to lift the rupiah back to the 8,000 level. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped prop up the rupiah over recent months by converting $5-15 million a day of aid and loan dollars into rupiah, usually through state banks. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's 1999/2000 budget assumes an average rupiah rate of 7,500 to the dollar. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1t05h1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
