\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 /Rupiah -2: Futile To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 1999\par 09:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--It would be futile for Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the rupiah against the dollar given that it's being hurt by external factors, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Sjahril Sabirin, said Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It's not right if we fight the market, as (the rupiah is weaker) because of external factors," Sjahril told reporters, adding that concerns that China would devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, had hit the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were rattled on Monday by speculation that China would devalue the yuan following Brazil's decision last week to let the real float freely. \par \par \uc2  A series of Chinese pledges not to devalue - including a promise by Chinese premier, Zhu Rongji, Monday not to weaken the Chinese unit this year - have gone some way towards quashing market fears. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1q00lr9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
