\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Lower On Offshore Selling Pressure \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1999\par 11:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah bucked the trend of some other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region Thursday, ending Asian trade lower against the dollar, largely the result of pressure from offshore participants to push the rupiah down. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quite volatile," said a trader with a foreign bank in Jakarta. "Some Singapore buyers tried to squeeze the market to push the rupiah lower." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah (IDR) was quoted at IDR8,675 to the U.S. dollar at the end of the day, down from IDR8,470 late Wednesday in Singapore. The Jakarta market was closed Wednesday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the locals are still on holidays; this was the offshore players," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Many Indonesians are on vacation this week following the two day muslim Idul Fitri holidays Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said offshore participants had sought to push the rupiah lower citing outbreaks of rioting and unrest in some parts of the country. \par \par \uc2  Religious violence spread in eastern Indonesia on Thursday when rioting among Christians and Muslims flared for a third straight day. At least 24 people were killed in bloody clashes on two islands and fighting erupted on a third, police said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the rupiah. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week that it would step into the market if necessary, but there has been no evidence of this. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's auction of one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes Thursday resulted in an increase in interest rates, marking the second consecutive week of an increase in one-month rates after months of steady decline. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said allowing interest rates to rise was the more likely route Bank Indonesia would take in order to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "We don't see any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment," said the trader at the foreign bank. "I guess one of the ways to slow down the weakening of the rupiah is to let rates rise." \par \par \uc2  -By Grainne McCarthy; 6221 350 01 45; gmccarthy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1034GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1l00ies\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
