\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Ease After Two-Day Holiday \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1999\par 03:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates are slightly lower Thursday on ample liquidity as the demand for funds eases after the two-day Muslim Idul Fitri holiday. \par \par \uc2  At 0221 GMT, the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was at 30%, lower than the average of 34% last week during which strong demand for rupiah-denominated funds for the holiday pushed up market rates. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was flush with liquidity Thursday because banks last week did not aggressively bid for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes at the weekly auction. \par \par \uc2  Instead, they kept the rupiah funds handy in anticipation of the pre-holiday demand for cash. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set the daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rates, part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb excess funds, at levels close to the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is 29% for overnight funds, 32% for four to six days and 33% for seven-day funds. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its weekly auction of one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes today (Thursday) with a target amount of IDR12.7 trillion. \par \par \uc2  The auction was postponed from Wednesday because of the Idul Fitri holiday. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the dollar was fetching IDR8,600, up from IDR8,470 late Wednesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore swap market, the premium on the overnight forward contract was IDR5.5/6.6, reflecting an implied interest rate of about 29% to 30%, close to the market level while the one-month premium was at IDR230/270. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; 6221-350-0145; nfung@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0247GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1l00hvr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
