\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia stands firm despite Brazil. \b0\par\par\uc2 899 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 12:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 15 (Reuters) - Mounting concern that Brazil will be forced into a further real devaluation sent a shiver through many emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday although Asian markets were shielded by a sagging U.S. dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "I think we're beyond the stage where you going to get a full blown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis in Asia just as a result of Brazil," said Tim Fox, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar has been affected more than anything and this in a sense protecting the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Fox. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real remained near the top of its new trading band at just under 1.32 per dollar on Friday but the market was expecting further pressure when U.S. markets opened. \par \par \uc2  Media reports estimated between $1.5 billion and $1.8 billion left Brazil on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Capital flight depletes the country's vital foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - used to defend the real and pay foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt - and makes a further devaluation or a move to a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more likely, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar fell across the board in early European trade as traders speculated about the effects of another Brazilian real devaluation on U.S. economic and financial links with Latin America's largest economy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia were generally insulated by the yen's firmer tone of around 112 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwanese dollar and the Korean won saw small gains although the Thai baht and the Philippine peso weakened slightly against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A firmer yen has allowed the crisis-hit region to lower interest rates sharply over recent months. \par \par \uc2  "Asia's economies have undergone much of the reform that Brazil is now charged with although you can make an argument that interest rates there have some room to be back up in some cases," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The big loser among Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the Indonesian rupiah which slid through the 9,000 per dollar level to around 9,200, equalling an early November low. \par \par \uc2  The governor of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the bank may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupiah above the 8,000 per dollar mark. \par \par \uc2  But traders said no government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been seen yet and the market was eyeing the possibility of fresh unrest after next week's Eid al-Fitr holidays. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's 1999/2000 fiscal year budget forecasts an average rupiah rate of 7,500 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The South African rand, seen as vulnerable to Brazilian jitters due to the country's weak curent account position, held at weaker early levels after recovering from a four-month low of 6.33 per dollar in New York trade. \par \par \uc2  Eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally weaker with the polish zloty opening at 5.31/4.94 firmer than its trading band centre versus 6.45/6.25 in late Thursday trade. \par \par \uc2  The zloty can fluctuate in a band of 12.5 percent either side of its parity rate, set daily by the centrak bank based on a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket comprising 55 percent of the euro and 45 percent of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown opened weaker and was seen trading in a narrow range of between 35.8 to 36.2, local traders said. \par \par \uc2    ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, \par \par \uc2  including the change versus late New York trade the previous day \par \par \uc2  and the change in the year to date. \par \par \uc2   ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly \par \par \uc2  quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to \par \par \uc2  reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2   ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in \par \par \uc2  units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the \par \par \uc2  rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. \par \par \uc2   ** Annual percentage changes are now calculated from late on \par \par \uc2  the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab     "LATEST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 "    "PREV CLOSE" PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab    0N YEAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Czech Rep.\tab \tab    35.90\tab     35.87   0.11%     3.17%\par   Poland\tab \tab \tab   4.16\tab      4.16   0.11%     2.25%\par   Hungary\tab \tab      253.15\tab    253.10   0.02%     0.78%\par   Slovakia\tab \tab      42.78\tab     42.75   0.05%    -0.52%\par   Romania\tab \tab      11,300\tab    11,275   0.22%     3.20%\par   Ukraine\tab \tab \tab  4.13\tab      4.15  -0.48%     5.09%\par   South Africa\tab \tab   6.22\tab      6.31  -1.43%     6.45%\par   Kenya\tab \tab \tab   61.35\tab     61.10   0.41%    -0.41%\par   Israe