\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals weak but off lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 10:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0850 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly easier in \par \par \uc2  late trade despite the yen's firmer tone against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      But trade was thin, with Japan closed for a holiday and \par \par \uc2  widespread uncertainty over the impact of Brazil's devaluation. \par \par \uc2      Traders are increasingly nervous that Brazil might be \par \par \uc2  forced to float its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following a Standard & Poor's \par \par \uc2  ratings downgrade and as net dollar outflows reached an \par \par \uc2  estimated $1.14 billion on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But for the time being, Asian stock markets kept their \par \par \uc2  composure despite Wall Street's 2.45 percent drop and that \par \par \uc2  helped limit losses in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *** The dollar was easier as traders began to speculate on \par \par \uc2  the possibility of a U.S. interest rate cut if the Dow \par \par \uc2  continued to be pummelled by concerns about Brazil. \par \par \uc2      But dealers expected dollar bids to resurface near 112 yen \par \par \uc2  due to lingering fears of Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah remained weak after sliding through the \par \par \uc2  9,000 per dollar level as traders worried about the possibility \par \par \uc2  of fresh unrest after next week's Eid al-Fitr holidays. \par \par \uc2      It reached a low of 9,200, its lowest since November 5, and \par \par \uc2  traders expected further falls amid concerns of a delay in \par \par \uc2  June's planned general election if parliament fails to push \par \par \uc2  through political reform laws in time. \par \par \uc2      Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed to step in and defend \par \par \uc2  the rupiah, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet to be seen. \par \par \uc2      Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Syahril Sabirin has said the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would seek to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupiah firmer \par \par \uc2  than 8,000 to the dollar. Indonesia's budget for the 1999/2000 \par \par \uc2  fiscal year forecasts an average rupiah rate of 7,500. \par \par \uc2  *** The Korean won stood out with a small gain as local \par \par \uc2  companies unwound dollar positions in the face of a rising yen \par \par \uc2  and the local stock market's resilience to Wall Street's drop. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the number of firms whose bank \par \par \uc2  accounts were closed after defaulting on their debt dropped to \par \par \uc2  862 in December from 903 in November and 3,197 a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  It attributed the decline to the improving financial health \par \par \uc2  of local firms due to falling interest rates and increased \par \par \uc2  lending to small and medium-sized companies. \par \par \uc2  *** The Singapore dollar was also higher, largely because \par \par \uc2  of an unwinding of the long baht/short Sing positions put on in \par \par \uc2  recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The low level of interest rates in Singapore prompted \par \par \uc2  investors to borrow Singapore dollars and convert them to other \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and much of this cheap funding went on in Sing/baht. \par \par \uc2      Singapore corporates have also been seen buying into \par \par \uc2  Thailand. \par \par \uc2      *** The baht was some 0.5 percent down from late Thursday \par \par \uc2  levels on that cross play with the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said local commercial bank lending was \par \par \uc2  expected to grow by seven percent this year. Latest data show a \par \par \uc2  5.3 percent year-on-year contraction in bank lending for the \par \par \uc2  first 11 months of 1998. \par \par \uc2  Foreign reserves rose to $29.8 billion as at January 8 from \par \par \uc2  $29.5 billion on December 30. The Bank of Thailand said it had \par \par \uc2  net forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales contracts of $6.2 billon to \par \par \uc2  buy Thai baht as at January 8, against $6.6 billion on December \par \par \uc2  30. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day FRI 15 0850GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8890.00......8600.00........-3.26% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.10........36.90........-0.54% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.62........38.48........-0.36% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6795.......1.6840.........0.27% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.165.......32.210.........0.14% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1182.00......1184.50.........0.21% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....112.62.......113.85.........1.09% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8890.00......2432.00........-72.64% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.10........25.90........-30.19% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.62........26.50........-31.38% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6795.......1.4300........-14.86%