\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah ends weaker but bounces back from 9,000/dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah mounted a late fightback on Friday from a low of 9,250 against the dollar but still ended weaker with dealers predicting fresh attacks on the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a market holiday next week. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 8,800/8,900 in late Jakarta trade compared with 8,675/8,725 late on Thursday. It began the week at around 8,000. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia will not be running clearing and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and is closed on Tuesday and Wednesday, but dealers said more pressure on the rupiah was likely when the market re-opened. \par \par \uc2  "We all know that the problems in Brazil so far are the tip of the iceberg. But in Indonesia we also have so much uncertainty, there is the chance of messy elections, and this is contributing to very negative sentiment," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen some panic dollar buying and this could get worse." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a three-month low of 9,250 before clawing back some ground, though dealers said there had been no sign of significant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  propping up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The state banks came in around lunchtime, but they did not release a significant amount of dollars. The recovery we have seen was really more a technical retracement, but we expect further weakness next week," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said this week's weakness had been sparked by financial instability in Brazil, but magnified by growing concerns about Indonesia's political stability as crime and unrest spiral and a general election looms. \par \par \uc2  Talk that parliamentary deadlock over new election laws could cause a delay in the election added to the rupiah's weakness. The head of the government-appointed team in charge of the election laws later said there was no chance elections would be delayed. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that if 9,200 was breached again, the next resistance would be at 9,700 and then the psychological 10,000 level. \par \par \uc2  "If 10,000 goes, then you've got 15,000," one dealer said. "There would be panic buying of dollars, much more than we've seen already." \par \par \uc2  Dealers say concerns that violence and instability will increase in the run-up to elections will cast a shadow over the rupiah in the months ahead. \par \par \uc2  Students, behind much of the anti-government protests which helped topple former President Suharto in May and which caused mayhem in the capital late last year, have already pledged to hit the streets again from next week. \par \par \uc2  There are also concerns that a row between parliament and the government over the country's 1999/2000 budget could scupper desperately needed economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been helping support the rupiah for months by converting millions of dollars in foreign loans and aid to rupiah. It has been converting $5-15 million a day. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia Governor Syahril Sabirin said on Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would seek to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupiah firmer than 8,000 to the dollar. Indonesia's budget for the 1999/2000 fiscal year forecasts an average rupiah rate of 7,500. \par \par \uc2  But there was little sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be waiting until the initial storm subsides before stepping in to try and nudge the rupiah higher. They also pointed out that the inflow of funds the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been converting may be running dry. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1f06fj0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
