\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 -3: Philippine Peso Claws Back Early Loss \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 10:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Some market participants suggested that, rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may instead attempt to bolster the rupiah by pushing up local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Throughout December short-term interest rates, as represented by the rate on one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes, have held steady at around 35%. Should pressure on the rupiah increase, however, Bank Indonesia may be prepared to push that rate up to around 45%, suggested one Jakarta-based trader, despite the adverse effects on Indonesia's corporate sector. \par \par \uc2  Although other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Philippine peso and the Thai baht, also suffered from Brazil-induced jitters at the start of the day, by the end of Asian trading they had recovered most, if not all, their earlier losses. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System the peso came under heavy pressure early in the session, but later clawed back the bulk of its losses to finish the day only slightly lower against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Acknowledging that the turmoil in Brazil is likely to dent investor confidence in emerging markets, including the Philippines, a senior Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Dow Jones Newswires: "The Philippine economy is in good shape to withstand the contagion." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, is prepared to raise interest rates to defend the peso, should the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  come under further pressure as a result of the real devaluation. \par \par \uc2  At the close of local trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at PHP38.500, up from PHP38.460 at Wednesday's close, but well down from Thursday's intraday high of PHP38.850. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0956GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00baw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
