\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals weak in early trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 826 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 02:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0010 GMT - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were showing an easier bias in \par \par \uc2  early deals as the dollar firmed slightly against the yen, \par \par \uc2  though the market remained nervous about driving it down \par \par \uc2  sharply following the Bank of Japan's (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin repeated his \par \par \uc2  preference for a strong dollar overnight, saying it had \par \par \uc2  underpinned the still solid U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2      He dismissed suggestions that the administration had been \par \par \uc2  willing to let the dollar slip against the yen to help \par \par \uc2  embattled U.S. manufacturing and steel industries out of a \par \par \uc2  bind. \par \par \uc2      His remarks helped lift the dollar, but analysts said the \par \par \uc2  dollar could face further downside in the face of continuing \par \par \uc2  concerns about Brazil and Japanese repatriations ahead of the \par \par \uc2  fiscal year end in March. \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht was among the worst hit by the yen's \par \par \uc2  fall, with worries the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might buy dollars to settle \par \par \uc2  its forward obligations contributing to its soft tone. \par \par \uc2      Signs of further interest rate cuts at Thai banks also \par \par \uc2  weighed on the baht, with Krung Thai Bank announcing a 50 basis \par \par \uc2  point lending rate cut, effective today. \par \par \uc2      This brings its minimum lending rate to 11.25 percent and \par \par \uc2  its minimum retail and overdraft rates to 11.75 percent. \par \par \uc2      Bank of Asia cut its its minimum lending rate to 13.25 \par \par \uc2  percent from 13.75 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's main opposition New Aspiration Party is due to \par \par \uc2  submit censure motions in parliament against Finance Minister \par \par \uc2  Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda and two other top ministers. \par \par \uc2      Tarrin will be questioned in a parliamentary debate at the \par \par \uc2  end of the month for alleged lack of transparency in managing \par \par \uc2  the sales of assets belonging to closed finance companies. \par \par \uc2      Analysts see little actual political risk in Thailand, but \par \par \uc2  the launch of the censure motions is likely to keep markets a \par \par \uc2  bit edgy. \par \par \uc2      The state-run Financial Restructuring Authority signed \par \par \uc2  contracts to sell some 156 billion baht of financial and \par \par \uc2  commercial assets left by 56 defunct finance firms with seven \par \par \uc2  groups of bidders. \par \par \uc2  *** The Korean won also took a bit of a knock from the \par \par \uc2  yen's fall, fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Korea \par \par \uc2  and profit-taking in the stock market. \par \par \uc2      Seoul stocks started firm, but quickly headed south as \par \par \uc2  investors took profit on recent gains. \par \par \uc2      Commerce Minister Park Tae-young said Korea's economy was \par \par \uc2  expected to return to robust growth of five percent in 2000 as \par \par \uc2  economic restructuring takes effect. \par \par \uc2      Park said 1998 GDP showed an estimated 6.1 percent \par \par \uc2  contraction from the previous year, but was expected to return \par \par \uc2  to growth of 2.1 percent this year. \par \par \uc2      The government has officially projected 1999 full-year \par \par \uc2  growth at 2.0 percent, but an internal \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  report has \par \par \uc2  estimated growth will be as high as 3.2 percent. \par \par \uc2      Park also said the trade surplus would begin shrinking from \par \par \uc2  1999 due to a rise in imports as the economy picks up. This \par \par \uc2  year's trade surplus is projected to reach $25 billion from a \par \par \uc2  provisional $39.9 billion in 1998. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah fell further as dollar demand picked up \par \par \uc2  ahead of next week's Moslem Eid al-Fitr festivities, but \par \par \uc2  dealers said thin volumes and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would limit its decline. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would temporarily allow \par \par \uc2  banks to extend credits to non-affiliated parties up to a \par \par \uc2  maximum of 30 percent of their capital from 20 percent \par \par \uc2  previously. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was easing the restriction to help \par \par \uc2  banks cope with the economic crisis, and the new ruling applies \par \par \uc2  to credits extended between end-December 1998 and the end of \par \par \uc2  2001. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 13 0100GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8220.00......8000.00.........-2.68% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.63........36.35.........-0.76% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.98........37.87.........-0.29% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6860.......1.6790.........-0.42% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.160.......32.170..........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1173.00......1172.00.........-0.09% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....112.35..