\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah falls through 8,000, support seen at 8,100. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 10:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 11 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened through 8,000 to the dollar on Tuesday but dealers said it was unlikely to fall below 8,100 due to expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in at that level to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 8,025/8,055 in late Jakarta trade compared with 7,940/8,040 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We saw demand from local and especially state banks today, buying dollars again, and that pushed the rate over 8,000," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "We still see 8,100 as being well held because of fears that the central bnak might step in." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there had been higher demand for dollars in recent weeks to cover increased imports ahead of the Moslem festival of Eid al-Fitr on January 19/20, but this had already been largely satisfied. \par \par \uc2  They said the market was likely to remain quiet in the run up to the festival. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia Governor Syahril Sabirin said on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to step in to defend the rupiah if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We are trying our best to make it stable. If some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary we will do so. We do not want to see the rate fluctuate in a wider band," he told Reuters Television in Hong Kong ahead of a meeting of central bankers. \par \par \uc2  "But in my view the current rate can be sustained," Sabirin said. "There is still room for the exchange rate to be stronger than the current level but the current level already is all right." \par \par \uc2  For months the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been converting around $5-15 million a day in aid and loan dollars into rupiah. Analysts say this has been a significant factor in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's budget for the fiscal year to end-March 2000, released last week, assumes an average exchange rate of 7,500 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Because of thin market conditions and a lack of speculative traders, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be extremely effective in supporting the rupiah, analysts say. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06n4z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
