\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah slips but clings to 8,000 level as '98 ends. \b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1998\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 30 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah came under fresh pressure in the final hours of 1998 trade on Wednesday but clung to 8,000 to the dollar, boosted by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledge to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against further weakness, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted in late Jakarta trade at 7,990/8,090 after trading in a range of 7,900 to 8,100 through the day - well above the January and June lows of 17,000 but still a long way from its 1997 close of 5,300. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers and analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slide in the months ahead. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin told reporters the monetary authorities would try to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening below 8,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The comments by the governor that they want to maintain the rupiah below 8,000 caused some dollar selling, but there was no follow-through from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so people eventually recovered their positions again," said a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been converting $10-15 million a day in aid and loan dollars into rupiah in recent months, giving the beleaguered Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a significant boost in the thin market conditions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists this does not constitute \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But dealers say Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the rupiah when it comes under pressure, sometimes selling large amounts of dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Sabirin's comments could signal a more openly pro-active stance on the part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah. Officials have said the budget for Indonesia's 1999/2000 fiscal year assumes an exchange rate of 7,000 to 8,000. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's top economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita said earlier this month that the rupiah could strengthen beyond 7,000 to the dollar once parliamentary elections scheduled for June are out of the way. \par \par \uc2  But many analysts believe the rupiah is headed lower, citing concern about unrest ahead of the elections and the possibility of a liquidity explosion as Indonesia struggles to pay for its budget commitments and fund an ambitious bank recapitalisation programme. \par \par \uc2  Chartists say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be slipping out of its recent range of 7,500 to 8,000 rupiah and this could signal a slide towards 9,000. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market sentiment is that the rupiah will weaken again come next year," one dealer said. "But my view is that yes it will weaken but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be keeping an eye on it. I don't think that during the month of Ramadhan you will see major fluctuations." ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926ducu01m20\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
