\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia c.bank says will try to halt rupiah fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1998\par 05:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 30 (Reuters) - Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said on Wednesday the country's monetary authorities would try to prevent the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling below 8,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We must try," Sabirin told reporters when asked whether the authorities would try to prevent the rupiah from falling below 8,000. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has weakened to around 8,000 against the dollar in early trading on Wednesday from around 7,600 early last week. \par \par \uc2  Sabirin said the rupiah's weakness was temporary and largely due to year-end and Eid al-Fitr Moslem celebrations. \par \par \uc2  In recent months the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been converting $10-15 million a day of aid and loan dollars into rupiah, giving the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a significant boost in thin market conditions. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists the conversion should not be regarded as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But some dealers and analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , converting larger amounts of dollars to support the rupiah when it comes under pressure. ((Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926ducu01l1r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
