\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Lower On Improved Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1998\par 02:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates fell slightly early Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected a large amount of funds into the system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia injected 5.319 trillion rupiah (IDR) ($1=IDR7,800) into the money market early Friday. The injection was the result of the expiration of Sertifikat Bank Indonesia (SBI), Bank Indonesia's short-term notes. \par \par \uc2  At 0128 GMT (8:28 p.m. EST), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was down to 30%-32% from between 32% and 35% a day earlier for foreign banks, and fell to between 31% and 33% from 35%-36% for secured local banks. \par \par \uc2  "With the amount injected into the system, liquidity should be flush," said a dealer with a local bank. "But interest rates are still slightly higher than early this week on anticipation of increasing demand from the rupiah ahead of year end." \par \par \uc2  Dealers mentioned that the International Monetary Fund's warning that Indonesia should not let interest rates fall drastically also provided support to interbank interest rates. \par \par \uc2  To absorb excess liquidity, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by borrowing rupiah from the market for three days tenure only. Its borrowing rate is at 28%. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar was trading at IDR7,800, unchanged from its close Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana (62-21) 3500145 imsentana@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-12-98 \par \par \uc2  01