\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Down On Flush Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1998\par 03:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money-market rates were mostly sharply lower Thursday, as liquidity expanded after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned down many bids at its weekly note auction Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, forecast interest rates to rise slowly, as demand for the rupiah is expected to increase ahead of the year-end. \par \par \uc2  At 0143 GMT (8:43 p.m. Wednesday EST), the benchmark overnight interbank rate was down to around 29% for foreign and joint-venture banks, down from around 33% a day earlier. Meanwhile, big local banks are obtaining overnight rupiah at interest rates between 30% and 35%, compared to between 33% and 38% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In a weekly auction Wednesday, Bank Indonesia accepted only 61% of the total bids for the one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia (SBI) notes, and 87% of the total bids for three-month maturities. \par \par \uc2  The one-month SBI yielded 37.86%, down from 42.42% at last week's auction. \par \par \uc2  "Many participants bids for much higher yields, and many got turned down," a dealer said. "As a result, the market is flush with liquidity Thursday." \par \par \uc2  A net injection of 4.06 trillion rupiah (IDR) by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day boosted liquidity further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In order to absorb liquidity back from the market, as well as to prevent a sharp decline in interest rates, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by borrowing rupiah from the market early Thursday for overnight tenure only. The rate is pegged at 29%, unchanged from Tuesday. It didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets early Thursday, the dollar was trading at IDR7,500, unchanged from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the swap market meanwhile, premiums were mostly lower, as the market expects Indonesian interest rates to fall further, especially next year. The most notable decline was on the six- and nine-month swap premiums, which fell to between 22% and 28%, from between 27% and 29% Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana (62-21) 3500145 imsentana@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-12-98 \par \par \uc2  0240GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duca01xdn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
