\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah edges down, braced for fresh demonstrations. \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1998\par 04:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The rupiah edged lower on Friday with dealers saying the market was nervous about fresh protests in Jakarta a week after violent clashes in the capital left at least 14 dead and turned the business district into a battlezone. \par \par \uc2  By 0240 GMT the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 7,525/7,625 compared with 7,425/7,525 at the close in Jakarta on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said most players were expected to square their positions and shut up shop early to avoid expected protests in the business district around Atma Jaya university, where nine students died last week in clashes with the security forces. \par \par \uc2  "The market is cautious about students on the streets. Today is the seventh day after the students died and probably there will be crowds again in the Atma Jaya area," said one dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was largely unaffected by last week's unrest, and some dealers said they suspected Bank Indonesia had been converting an increased amount of aid and loan dollars into rupiah to prop it up. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia says it has been converting $5-15 million a day of aid and loan dollars into rupiah in recent months, giving the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a significant boost in a market where daily volume rarely exceeds $200 million. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed up to $50 million a day last week to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists it is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and says its selling of dollars for rupiah is purely to meet budgetary needs and satisfy the market's dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  Dennis de Tray, the World Bank's country director for Indonesia, said on Thursday recent gains by the rupiah were "real" and not the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The important, underlined piece of information on the exchange rate...is that the recent strengthening of the rupiah, contrary to what you may have read, is not being driven by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told a conference in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  He said the International Monetary Fund, which closely monitored such matters, had told him the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not been boosted by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "But also data on foreign reserves, published regularly, simply does not support the story of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384 6364; Fax +6221 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubk0422o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
