\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  not behind rupiah gains - World Bank. \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1998\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Recent gains by the rupiah are "real" and not the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the World Bank's country director for \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The important, underlined piece of information on the exchange rate...is that the recent strengthening of the rupiah, contrary to what you may have read, is not being driven by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Dennis de Tray told a conference in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  He said the International Monetary Fund, which closely monitored such matters, had told him the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not been boosted by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "But also data on foreign reserves, published regularly, simply does not support the story of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it is changing around $5 million to $15 million a day of foreign aid and loans into rupiah, a significant amount in a market where daily volume rarely reaches $200 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists the conversion should not be considered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has climbed from a low of 17,000 per dollar in June to around 7,500 now, and held its ground over the last week despite violent clashes on the streets of Jakarta which left at least 14 dead. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts have said the rupiah's recent stability was due to Bank Indonesia converting an increased amount of dollars into rupiah. \par \par \uc2  De Tray said that after adjusting for inflation, the rupiah had depreciated by around 40 percent since July 1997, "comparable to the level of depreciation in December 1997, before Indonesia entered serious political crisis". This was a positive sign, he said. \par \par \uc2  But he warned that continued recovery required political stability. \par \par \uc2  "The economy is beginning to mend but it won't hold if the politics don't hold," he said. "Indonesia must decide whether it will hold together or fall apart." ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384 6364; Fax +6221 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubj0484x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
