\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Ginandjar -3: Sees Miyazawa Plan Helping Economy \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1998\par 04:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The violence that hit the capital last week was the worst since May, when much heavier rioting and looting swept the city and helped unseat President Suharto after three decades in power. \par \par \uc2  The minister also reiterated comments that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the rupiah, and attributed the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to global interest rate cuts, a stronger Japanese yen and the strength of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  He did confirm, however, that Bank Indonesia is converting international aid funds into rupiah in the money markets. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't regard this as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , arguing that it needs to buy rupiah to finance the shortfall of the state budget. \par \par \uc2  "Strong economic growth requires some supporting indicators," he said. "For instance, the recent rate cuts in the U.S. and some European countries and the stronger yen have become positive supporting factors for the Indonesian economy." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Open Market Committee Tuesday announced a quarter-percentage point cut in both its fed funds and its discount interest rate, making it the third cut in interest rates in seven weeks. \par \par \uc2  Ginandjar referred to Japan's $30 billion Miyazawa plan to stimulate the Asian economies in need as something that would help bring growth in the region. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0343GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubj01b22\par }\page {\par\fs20{