\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah ends stronger on offshore dollar selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1998\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah firmed on Wednesday, vaulting 8,000 to the dollar on overseas dollar selling despite more clashes on the streets of Jakarta, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended at 7,700/7,800 to the dollar after closing at 8,100/8,200 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Offshore dollar selling, particularly out of Singapore, had bolstered the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian troops fired warning shots in the air as they tried to block students marching towards parliament, where a special session of the country's highest legislative body, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), is taking place. \par \par \uc2  There were no serious injuries but some students were hurt in scuffles with troops. \par \par \uc2  The four-day assembly meeting, which got under way on Tuesday, will discuss political reforms and bring forward parliamentary elections to next year from 2002. But student protesters say the MPR is a leftover from the now-discredited regime of former President Suharto. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar selling by state banks also lent support to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to increase conversion of aid dollars into rupiah this week to boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid worries of fresh unrest as the MPR met. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has been converting $10-15 million a day of aid and loan dollars into rupiah in recent months, giving the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a significant boost in the thin market conditions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was widely thought to have been behind offshore dollar selling on Tuesday, triggering stop-loss dollar selling by other operators and pulling the rupiah upwards. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists it is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and says its selling of dollars for rupiah is purely to meet budgetary needs and satisfy the market's dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rates for its one and three-month paper did not have much impact on the rupiah as it had largely been expected. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's weekly auction of its one-month SBI certificates on Wednesday resulted in a weighted average interest rate of 51.16 percent against 53.66 percent last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said. \par \par \uc2  The bank said the monthly auction of its three-month SBI paper resulted in a weigthed interest rate of 50.49 percent against 58.71 percent last month. ((Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubb04vmu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
