\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah gains, breaks 8,000 on offshore dlr selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1998\par 03:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah advanced in early trade on Wednesday on offshore dollar selling, breaking through 8,000 to the dollar and trading as high as 7,800 despite the risk of more clashes on the streets of Jakarta, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said early dollar selling out of Singapore had bolstered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but could not say whether Bank Indonesia was behind the trades. \par \par \uc2  "There has been some selling this morning, so far just by Singapore players," said one dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. "We don't know whether BI is behind it." \par \par \uc2  By 0120 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 7,700/7,900 to the dollar, after closing at 8,100 in Jakarta on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a firmer yen had also lent the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  some support, though the rupiah was mainly moving independently of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's highest legislative body, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), is holding a four-day special session to ratify the country's election timetable and discuss laws which President B.J. Habibie says will promote democracy. \par \par \uc2  Thousands of student protesters took to the streets on Tuesday, and sporadic clashes broke out with pro-government security volunteers armed with sticks and sharpened canes who had vowed to protect the assembly session. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the threat of renewed unrest on Wednesday was keeping the market on edge despite its gains, but added the expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to prop up the rupiah if it began to slide would give the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  some support. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah was fairly resilient yesterday despite the trouble in Jakarta," said a dealer at a Japanese bank in Jakarta. "That was partly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support, but it has put some people's worries at rest." \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has been converting $10-15 million a day of aid and loan dollars into rupiah in recent months, giving the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a significant boost in the thin market conditions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up the amount of dollars being converted into rupiah if nervousness about the assembly meeting hits the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was widely thought to have been behind offshore dollar selling on Tuesday, triggering stop-loss dollar selling by other operators and pulling the rupiah upwards. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists it is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and says its selling of dollars for rupiah is purely to meet budgetary needs and satisfy the market's dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues aggressively selling (dollars), we could see the rupiah break 8,000 and even move to 7,500," one dealer said. "But we still have to wait until Friday until we see the result of the MPR and whether it will satisfy the students and other political parties." \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia holds an auction on Wednesday of one-month and three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper. It has targeted absorbing eight trillion rupiah with the one-month paper and two trillion rupiah with three-month paper. Results are expected around 0900 GMT. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384 6364; Fax +6221 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubb04ub4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
