\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah ends firmer despite assembly nerves. \b0\par\par\uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1998\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah ended firmer on Tuesday, lifted by aggressive bidding by state banks and stop-loss selling by offshore operators despite concerns about clashes on the streets of Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke briefly through the 8,000 barrier, trading as high as 7,950, with dealers saying \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar selling had again helped boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended in Jakarta at 8,100 to the dollar, compared with 8,500/8,600 in early trade and 8,425/8,525 at the close of Jakarta dealings on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We saw some stop-loss selling by banks in Singapore," said a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "After lunch some state banks were offering (dollars) in the market on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's highest legislative body, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), began a four-day special session to ratify the country's election timetable and discuss laws which President B.J. Habibie says will promote democracy. \par \par \uc2  But markets are focused less on the political machinations inside Jakarta's parliament building than on events on the streets outside - where sporadic clashes broke out between pro-reform student protesters and Moslem groups armed with sticks who have vowed to protect the assembly. \par \par \uc2  In the rising tension that has surrounded the meeting, thousands of Indonesian student demonstrators and pro-government activists threw stones at each other in central Jakarta, but there were no reports of serious injuries. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore selling helped the rupiah shrug off the unrest. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen dollar selling in Hong Kong, mainly through interbank players," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "Some suspect that some of the selling in Hong Kong is on behalf of Bank Indonesia." \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said there were rumours Bank Indonesia had been selling more dollars than usual but this had not been confirmed. \par \par \uc2  "German names have been selling, but we don't know what's behind that," said the dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. "We don't know whether there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we still haven't been able to substantiate that." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been converting $10-15 million a day of aid and loan dollars into rupiah in recent months, giving the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a significant boost in the thin market conditions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said earlier this week they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up the amount of dollars being converted into rupiah if nervousness about the assembly meeting hit the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  insists it is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and says its selling of dollars for rupiah is purely to meet budgetary needs and satisfy the market's dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues aggressively selling (dollars), we could see the rupiah break 8,000 and even move to 7,500," one dealer said. "But we still have to wait until Friday until we see the result of the MPR and whether it will satisfy the students and other political parties." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was also boosted by comments from International Monetary Fund first deputy managing director Stanley Fischer, who said in a speech in Australia there was no reason why the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not move back to 7,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We guess that with the amount of inflation that has happened so far this year...if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to stop in the 6,500-7,000 or so (range) you would find yourself with a devaluation in real terms roughly similar to that in the other crisis countries of somewhere between 25 and 35 percent," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said it had targeted absorbing eight trillion rupiah with Wednesday's weekly auction of one-month SBI paper and two trillion rupiah with its monthly auction of three-month paper. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384 6364; Fax +6221 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duba04s6r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
