\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Indonesian newspapers - November 6. \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1998\par 02:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  The following are the leading stories in the Indonesian press on November 6. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  Telephone: (6221) 384-6364. Fax:(6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA POST \par \par \uc2  - Even as preparations for the special session of the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) shifted into high gear, groups of proponents and opponents staged "trial" demonstrations ahead of the November 10-13 session. \par \par \uc2  - The rupiah remained under pressure, breaking through the 9,000 barrier against the U.S. dollar before bouncing back to close at 8,600 after massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by state banks. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  KOMPAS \par \par \uc2  - Tens of thousands of Moslems gathered at a central Jakarta stadium to express their support for the coming special session of the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) next week. \par \par \uc2  - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be provoked into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the rupiah. Since the volume of transactions in rupiah/dollar is reaching $165-$200 million, its efforts could be wasted, said Theo Toemion of Speed \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . - - - - \par \par \uc2  BISNIS INDONESIA \par \par \uc2  - Garuda's managing director Robby Djohan is almost certain to leave his job at the airline to head Bank Mandiri, the newly formed bank which comprises four merged state-owned banks, said an official of the Ministry of State Enterprises. \par \par \uc2  - A speedy recapitalisation of banks would ensure that more than half of the country's troubled banks will survive, said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  REPUBLIKA \par \par \uc2  - Thousands of Moslems gathered at a stadium in central Jakarta, expressing support for the coming special session of the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) and issued a statement opposing groups who were against the session. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin said there was no need for the government to implement a managed floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system despite the weakening of the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  MEDIA INDONESIA \par \par \uc2  - Marzuki Darusman, the head of a fact-finding team charged with investigating the country's bloody mid-May riots, said it was up to the government to investigate a meeting at the headquarters of the military's strategic reserve forces on May 14 which was said to be linked to the violence which erupted. \par \par \uc2  - Garuda's managing director is expected to head Bank Mandiri following the stepping down of the bank's current managing director Mulyo Hardjoko. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404. \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dub605103\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
