\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Regionals have firm bias but Sing sags. \b0\par\par\uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1998\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a firmer overall \par \par \uc2  bias after a quiet session but the Singapore dollar and Korean \par \par \uc2  won edged lower. \par \par \uc2      Dollar/yen was little changed from its prevous Asian close \par \par \uc2  and still hanging around under the 120 level. \par \par \uc2      The dollar remained firm against the mark on speculation of \par \par \uc2  further rate cuts in Europe following the Bank of Italy's \par \par \uc2  surprise decision to slash interest rates on Monday. \par \par \uc2      *** Dealers expect a test of 120 yen likely in the near \par \par \uc2  term, especially if the dollar strengthens against mark. But \par \par \uc2  offers from Japanese exporters are seen lined up near that \par \par \uc2  level, and already there are signs of some profit taking \par \par \uc2  limiting the dollar's gains. \par \par \uc2  *** Some in the market are expecting a German rate cut \par \par \uc2  despite remarks by Bundesbank officials rejecting such calls. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank Vice President Juergen Stark, in a speech said: "The \par \par \uc2  recently expressed demands that the monetary policy should \par \par \uc2  loosen its reins to promote employment as well as calls for \par \par \uc2  more expansive fiscal policies are neither helpful nor \par \par \uc2  appropriate". \par \par \uc2      *** Changes in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were narrow with the \par \par \uc2  rupiah moving ahead only slightly. \par \par \uc2      Dealer's expect it to remain well with its current 7,000 to \par \par \uc2  8,000 range. \par \par \uc2      Bank Indonesia managing director Miranda Goeltom said on \par \par \uc2  Monday there were no plans to impose an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band on \par \par \uc2  the rupiah. "I have no idea about the rumours of an \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, and there is no such plan (for a band). We \par \par \uc2  are currently still focusing on the implementation of capital \par \par \uc2  (flow) monitoring," she told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Bisnis Indonesia daily reported on Monday that Bank \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would implement an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to control the \par \par \uc2  value of the rupiah. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said interest rates \par \par \uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates (SBIs) are expected to fall \par \par \uc2  further next week. \par \par \uc2  "(One-month) SBI rates have been gradually falling from 70 \par \par \uc2  percent to 58 percent and are seen falling again next week," \par \par \uc2  Sabirin told reporters. \par \par \uc2      He also said he saw the rupiah being stable ahead of the \par \par \uc2  November 10-13 government assembly session. \par \par \uc2      *** The Singapore dollar bucked the generally firmer trend \par \par \uc2  and looks vulnerable to renewed dollar strength with a decisive \par \par \uc2  push through 1.63 setting up a move lower. \par \par \uc2      *** Hong Kong's government said it made a hefty paper \par \par \uc2  profit with its unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market \par \par \uc2  last August. The government spent HK$118 billion ($15.2 \par \par \uc2  billion) on blue chips during its foray into the market. Its \par \par \uc2  portfolio, which includes all 33 companies listed in the Hang \par \par \uc2  Seng index, was worth HK$146.43 billion ($18.9 billion) at \par \par \uc2  closing prices on Monday, or about a 24 percent paper profit. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won also gave ground as corporations began \par \par \uc2  to cover their short positions. \par \par \uc2      *** The Taiwan dollar rose to a seven-month high amid \par \par \uc2  foreign fund inflows and dollar selling through non-delivery \par \par \uc2  forwards. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said foreign funds on Monday and Tuesday flowed in \par \par \uc2  for the stock market as foreign funds recently have been net \par \par \uc2  stock buyers. \par \par \uc2      They said importers now were hesitant to buy U.S. dollars \par \par \uc2  after seeing the Taiwan dollar's strong gains on Monday and in \par \par \uc2  early Tuesday trading. \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso stood out again with another strong \par \par \uc2  gain amid strong \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows. \par \par \uc2      Traders said there was a widespread belief that these \par \par \uc2  inflows would continue and speculative plays were being put on. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Change on the day TUE 27 0858GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7300.00......7400.00..........1.37% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.34........37.60..........0.70% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.88........41.60..........1.76% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6285.......1.6255.........-0.18% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.600.......32.735..........0.41% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1318.00......1313.00.........-0.38% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....119.22.......119.14.........-0.07% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgi