\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia rupiah edges higher, tone seen firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah edged higher against the dollar on Monday and dealers said sentiment on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to remain firm on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended at 7,400/7,500 against the dollar compared with 7,800/7,900 in Friday's Jakarta trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's rise was partly due to overeas dollar selling amid a thin market and a local newspaper report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might reimpose an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  Miranda Goeltom, a director with Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, denied the report and said the bank did not have plans to impose the band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said reimposing the band might not work best in the current volatile regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as players might be tempted to break the band which in turn could force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to abandon it again. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, said expected further conversion of aid dollars into rupiah and a relatively stable political situation were likely to keep sentiment firm on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duaq02lhz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
