\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Rupiah and peso gain, others steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 902 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 09:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0800 GMT - The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a quietly steady day \par \par \uc2  as dollar/yen held in a narrow range, but the rupiah firmed as \par \par \uc2  aid dollars flowed across the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2       Dollar/yen was little changed from Friday's late Asian \par \par \uc2  level but it was up a little on Friday's New York close. \par \par \uc2      Japan's still acute banking sector problems will tend to \par \par \uc2  prevent the yen moving any higher but for now most traders do \par \par \uc2  not see it dipping below the 120 per dollar level. \par \par \uc2      The dollar did get some support from news that European \par \par \uc2  leaders believe the conditions are right for interest rate \par \par \uc2  cuts. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah stood out with another good gain but its \par \par \uc2  recent rally does seem to be slowing and many in the market do \par \par \uc2  not see it moving substantially higher from here. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah has rallied some 35 percent this month and has \par \par \uc2  more than doubled in value against the dollar since its June \par \par \uc2  low of around 17,000. \par \par \uc2      The move higher has been fuelled by the conversion of aid \par \par \uc2  dollars into rupiah and despite the apparently spectacular \par \par \uc2  rally it is still almost 70 percent down on levels seen before \par \par \uc2  the Asia crisis kicked-off in July 1997. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \par \par \uc2  rupiah in coming months but will aim to create conditions which \par \par \uc2  prevent excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  "We will let the rupiah move in accordance with market \par \par \uc2  laws. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  director Achyar Iljas was quoted as saying by the official \par \par \uc2  Antara news agency. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah did gain some support from a local newspaper \par \par \uc2  report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might reimpose an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  *** In Malaysia trouble flared at the weekend with two \par \par \uc2  policemen and 12 protesters injured and 241 arrested as crowds \par \par \uc2  clashed with police. \par \par \uc2  Supporters of the detained former deputy prime minister \par \par \uc2  Anwar Ibrahim threw rocks and petrol bombs around a mosque in \par \par \uc2  the Moslem Kampong Bharu district. \par \par \uc2      Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad condemned his opponents \par \par \uc2  saying his government would not be intimidated. \par \par \uc2      Away from his political problems, Mahathir's budget on \par \par \uc2  Friday received only a lukewarm response from analysts. \par \par \uc2      There was some praise that it would help stimulate the \par \par \uc2  economy but there is concern over just how Malaysia would fund \par \par \uc2  its projected budget deficit of 6.1 percent of GDP in 1999. \par \par \uc2      Analysts say there is no way the funding for next year's \par \par \uc2  budget can come from domestic sources and foresee aid from \par \par \uc2  outside the country being necessary. \par \par \uc2      Mahathir proposed more than four billion ringgit ($1 \par \par \uc2  billion) be spent on the transport sector and offered tax cuts \par \par \uc2  for exporters, local manufacturers of consumer durables and \par \par \uc2  investors in unit trusts. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's Second Finance Minister Mustapa Mohamed said the \par \par \uc2  government will not have any problem funding a projected 1999 \par \par \uc2  budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  He told Reuters Television that capital controls imposed in \par \par \uc2  September have been a success, and Malaysia would consider the \par \par \uc2  competitiveness of its neighbours' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  before scrapping \par \par \uc2  the controls. \par \par \uc2  *** The peso was another bright spot on continued \par \par \uc2  speculation that dollars from direct investment will make their \par \par \uc2  way across the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was talk that proceeds from the sale of \par \par \uc2  San Miguel Corporation's stake in Nestle Philippines Inc and \par \par \uc2  Coca-Cola Beverages were finding their way into the market. \par \par \uc2  San Miguel sold its 45 percent stake in Nestle last August \par \par \uc2  for about $695 million. In July, it sold its stake in Coca-Cola \par \par \uc2  for 339.6 million sterling or around 24 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2      The Philippine Lower House on Sunday approved a proposed \par \par \uc2  1999 national budget of 579.5 billion pesos ($13.8 billion). \par \par \uc2      The proposed appropriation is 9.7 percent higher than this \par \par \uc2  year's budget and targets a lower budget deficit of 17.9 \par \par \uc2  billion pesos from this year's projected deficit of 40 billion \par \par \uc2  pesos. \par \par \uc2  The budget bill will go through a third reading for a final \par \par \uc2  vote when Congress reconvenes next month, although this is \par \par \uc2  considered a mere formality. \par \par \uc2  *** The Taiwan dollar closed at a seven-month high against \par \par \uc2  its U.S. counterpart amid U.S. dollar selling in form of \par \par \uc2  non-delivery forward and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won and the Singapore dollar both eased \par \par \uc2  slightly. \par \par \uc2      Singapore CPI fell 1.4% in September on a year-on-year \par \par \uc2  basis and was down 0.3% from August. This followed a 0.8% \par \par \uc2  year-on-year drop in August. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Change on the day MON 26 0816GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.8000.......3.8000.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7400.00......7650.00.........3.38% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.60........37.59........-0.03% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........41.60........41.90.........0.72% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6255.......1.6240........-0.09% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.735.......32.860.........0.38% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1313.00......1312.00........-0.08% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....119.14.......118.38........-0.64% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.8000.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7400.00......2432.00........-67.14% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.55........25.90........-31.03% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........41.60........26.50........-36.30% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6255.......1.4300........-12.03% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.7350......27.7500........-15.23% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1313.00.......842.00........-35.87% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....119.14.......114.40.........-3.98% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2   - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duaq02k