\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals little changed and quiet. \b0\par\par\uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 01:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0030 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  started the week on a \par \par \uc2  quiet note with most little changed from levels seen late last \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2      Traders expect a fairly slack week in terms of volume with \par \par \uc2  the market keeping one eye on dollar/yen and the other on \par \par \uc2  domestic factors. \par \par \uc2      The problem is that both are not giving any real direction \par \par \uc2  at the moment. \par \par \uc2      Dollar/yen was little changed from Friday's late Asian \par \par \uc2  level but it was up a little on Friday's New York close. \par \par \uc2      Japan's still acute banking sector problems will tend to \par \par \uc2  prevent the yen moving any higher but for now most traders do \par \par \uc2  not see it dipping below the 120 per dollar level. \par \par \uc2      News hat Daiwa Bank will withdraw from overseas banking \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by March 31, 2000 in order to focus on domestic \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no impact. \par \par \uc2      The dollar did get some support from news that European \par \par \uc2  leaders believe the conditions are right for interest rate \par \par \uc2  cuts. \par \par \uc2      Austrian Chancellor Viktor Klima, after a two-day informal \par \par \uc2  summit of EU heads of government, said the goal of economic \par \par \uc2  stability also required efforts to head off the threat of \par \par \uc2  deflation following financial turmoil across large parts of the \par \par \uc2  globe. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah was a touch firmer but its recent rally does \par \par \uc2  seem to be slowing and many in the market do not see it moving \par \par \uc2  substantially higher from here. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has rallied some 35 percent this month and has \par \par \uc2  more than doubled in value against the dollar since its June \par \par \uc2  low of around 17,000. \par \par \uc2  The move higher has been fuelled by the conversion of aid \par \par \uc2  dollars into rupiah and despite the apparently spectacular \par \par \uc2  rally it is still almost 70 percent down on levels seen before \par \par \uc2  the Asia crisis kicked-off in July 1997. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \par \par \uc2  rupiah in coming months but will aim to create conditions which \par \par \uc2  prevent excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  "We will let the rupiah move in accordance with market \par \par \uc2  laws. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  director Achyar Iljas was quoted as saying by the official \par \par \uc2  Antara news agency. \par \par \uc2  *** In Malaysia trouble flared at the weekend with two \par \par \uc2  policemen and 12 protesters injured and 241 arrested as crowds \par \par \uc2  clashed with police. \par \par \uc2  Supporters of the detained former deputy prime minister \par \par \uc2  Anwar Ibrahim threw rocks and petrol bombs around a mosque in \par \par \uc2  the Moslem Kampong Bharu district. \par \par \uc2      Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad condemned his opponents \par \par \uc2  saying his government would not be intimidated. \par \par \uc2      Away from his political problems, Mahathir's budget on \par \par \uc2  Friday received only a lukewarm response from analysts. \par \par \uc2      There was some praise that it would help stimulate the \par \par \uc2  economy but there is concern over just how Malaysia would fund \par \par \uc2  its projected budget deficit of 6.1 percent of GDP in 1999. \par \par \uc2      Analysts say there is no way the funding for next year's \par \par \uc2  budget can come from domestic sources and foresee aid from \par \par \uc2  outside the country being necessary. \par \par \uc2      Mahathir proposed more than four billion ringgit ($1 \par \par \uc2  billion) be spent on the transport sector and offered tax cuts \par \par \uc2  for exporters, local manufacturers of consumer durables and \par \par \uc2  investors in unit trusts. \par \par \uc2  *** The peso was little changed after rallying strongly on \par \par \uc2  Friday to three month highs, simply in anticipation of future \par \par \uc2  dollar demand. \par \par \uc2      The Philippine Lower House on Sunday approved a proposed \par \par \uc2  1999 national budget of 579.5 billion pesos ($13.8 billion). \par \par \uc2      The proposed appropriation is 9.7 percent higher than this \par \par \uc2  year's budget and targets a lower budget deficit of 17.9 \par \par \uc2  billion pesos from this year's projected deficit of 40 billion \par \par \uc2  pesos. \par \par \uc2  The budget bill will go through a third reading for a final \par \par \uc2  vote when Congress reconvenes next month, although this is \par \par \uc2  considered a mere formality. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duaq02kqs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
