\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah quiet after  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  control denials. \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1998\par 05:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was stable in quiet early trade on Wednesday with dealers satisified that the country was not poised to abandon its free-floating exchange rate system and impose \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls. \par \par \uc2  "Now the rumours about the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls have gone, the rupiah has stabilised," a dealer with a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 10,825/11,025 to the dollar at 0220 GMT on Wednesday, but did not trade through the 11,000 barrier. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the unit made substantial gains against the dollar as traders bought rupiah, anxious to close out positions and limit exposure to outstanding rupiah positions they would be unable to cover if controls were introduced. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 11,000/11,100 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia governor, Syahril Sabirin said there were no plans to abandon the free float, quashing the rumours. \par \par \uc2  "With no more rumours, there is no need to buy. I think we'll see the rupiah range-trading today and breaking 11,000 will be hard," a local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Traders are also waiting for the results of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly auction of its one-month certificates. The bank aims to absorb about 11 trillion rupiah in the auction. \par \par \uc2  The auction will give a sign on the likely direction of interest rates. Most in the market expect the weighted average interest rate of the SBI to be lower than last week's 69.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  "If the interest rate comes down, it will be a good sign for the economy. The market is looking for a fall," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier on Wednesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to fine tune short term monetary targets in daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had been lowered across the board. \par \par \uc2  - Nick Edwards (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9g016ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
