\par\par \b \uc2  Riot fears keep rupiah quiet in early trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The rupiah softened in early Friday trade with fears about possible weekend violence ahead of Indonesia's independence day keeping pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The risk is on the top side and if the riots happen, the rupiah is going to be a victim too," a dealer with one U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0220 GMT the rupiah was being traded around 13,000 against the dollar from an earlier high of 12,700, with dealers expecting a range of 12,900 to 13,100 to hold at least for the morning session. \par \par \uc2  "After lunch I'm not sure where we will go if the rumours about riots continue," a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at about the 13,000 level was also cited as a factor causing the rupiah to weaken. \par \par \uc2  "When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  went in, traders sold," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On the positive side, foreign traders were responding more warmly to the news that the interbank exchange of debt offer was progressing, after initial fears that the deal meant more bad news for Indonesian banks. \par \par \uc2  About US$2.7 billion of eligible external interbank debt of Indonesian banks scheduled to mature in the fiscal year ending March 31, 1999 will be exchanged for an equal amount of new loans guaranteed by Bank Indonesia with one, two, three and four-year maturities. \par \par \uc2  "People initially read this as defaulting, but now they realise it has international blessing, they are more relaxed about it," a dealer with a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  But hesitancy would remain through the day, dealers said, with the market set to react sharply to any news of unrest. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta Newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com ... \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e032z2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
