\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Up Late -2: Pushes Through Key Level \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 11:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah bounced up late Friday on aggressive selling of U.S. dollars by state-owned banks which overwrote lingering market fears about potential unrest this long weekend. \par \par \uc2  At 0916 GMT (5:16 a.m. EDT), the rupiah was quoted at IDR12,750 per U.S. dollar, much stronger than IDR12,950 traded late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported heavy selling of U.S. dollars by state banks around the key level of IDR13,000. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has been hovering around that level for the whole week and state banks have been seen actively offering dollars. But Friday's sale was seen as the most aggressive. \par \par \uc2  "They kept pushing the rupiah rate higher through to the intraday high of IDR12,650," a dealer at an American bank said. \par \par \uc2  He estimated the state banks spent about $30 million-$50 million during the day to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  All week, dealers have expressed uncertainty as to whether the state banks are acting on behalf of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or independently. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the money market to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0924GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8e06xzy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
