\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Slightly Higher Late On Debt Reschedule \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 13:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--he Indonesian rupiah ended the Asian day slightly higher Wednesday, cheered by the government's confirmation that it isn't unilaterally missing payments on its principal sovereign debt. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was fetching 13,000 rupiah (IDR) at the end of Asian trade, weaker than IDR13,200 the same time Tuesday. The rupiah is also sharply higher than IDR13,550 in offshore trade Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said trade remained thin, however. \par \par \uc2  "There's no demand really, the market's still very quiet," said the treasury chief with a local bank, adding that many investors were remaining clear of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of Indonesian Independence day on Monday, fearing potential uprest. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah weakened sharply Tuesday on the back of reports that the country had missed sovereign debt payments. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded, however, after Senior Economics Minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita said Indonesia had simply started to reschedule some of its debt in line with agreements with its major international lenders. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury Chief said state banks had offered to sell dollars at IDR13,100, but said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself hadn't been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  "We haven't detected anything from Bank Indonesia," he said. "We saw some selling from state banks but as usual aren't sure if they're acting for themselves or for Bank Indonesia." \par \par \uc2  The market also focused Wednesday on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 'sotes. \par \par \uc2  The bank raised IDR15.14 trillion rupiah at the third auction of its one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia, above its target of IDR13 trillion, a bank official said. \par \par \uc2  The auction of one-month notes raised IDR15.14 trillion at a weighted average rate of 69.5%, up from 68.3% last week. \par \par \uc2  The official said 95.1% of all bids were accepted. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is expected to trade within a tight range of IDR13,000-IDR13,200 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Grainne McCarthy; 6221 350 01 45; gmccarthy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1127GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 1131GMT) \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8c06vdp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
