\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Up Mid-Morning On Govt Debt Rescheduling \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 06:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah was slightly higher mid-morning Wednesday as the market welcomed the government's move to start rescheduling its sovereign debt in line with agreements with its major international lenders - and not unilaterally. \par \par \uc2  At 0315 GMT (11:15 p.m. EDT Tuesday), the rupiah was trading at 13,175 rupiah (IDR), up from IDR13,200 late Tuesday in Asian trading. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is stronger than IDR13,550 during London trade Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It has strengthened a lot compared to last night," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah weakened sharply Tuesday on the back of reports that the country had missed sovereign debt payments. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded, however, after senior economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita said Indonesia had simply started to reschedule some of its debt in line with agrerments with the International Monetary Fund, the Group of Seven and the Paris Club of Creditor Nations. \par \par \uc2  He stressed that Indonesia would continue to pay interest on its debt, as agreed with its lenders. \par \par \uc2  The trader said Ginandjar's commments helped inject confidence in the market. \par \par \uc2  He added that the move by state-owned banks to offer to sell dollars was also keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  "Earlier this morning, the state banks offered to sell U.S. dollars at IDR13,250 and then they offered to sell at IDR13,175," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He added that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself wasn't seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said Tuesday the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly and at the appropriate times to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer to sell IDR13 trillion of one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes later Wednesday with settlement Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Banks don't want to hold short positions knowing that the rupiah will be tighter ahead of the auction," said a dealer at a Singaporean bank. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is expected to trade within a tight range of IDR13,000 to IDR13,200 for the rest of the day. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; 6221-350-0150; nfung@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0407GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8c06tm0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
