\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Down Late On Weak Yen, China Yuan Concerns \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 12:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The weakening yen and continued concern over a possible devaluation of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have damped trading in the Indonesian rupiah Monday morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was excrutiatingly thin due to the closure of trading rooms in Singapore for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  "There was almost no interbank market because Singapore was closed," said a dealer with an American bank. \par \par \uc2  At 1040 GMT (6:40 a.m. EDT), the rupiah was quoted at 12,900 rupiah to the U.S. dollar, weaker than its Friday close of IDR12,750. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's movement was in line with the declining Japanese yen, which broke through Y146 to the dollar Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We are a bit concerned that the yen will trigger a devaluaton in China," said a dealer with an American bank. \par \par \uc2  The weak yen has sent ripples through the rest of the region, bringing the spotlight to the Chinese yuan and the Hong Kong dollar as speculation of a possible devaluation of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mounts. \par \par \uc2  State-owned banks were seen offering U.S. dollars at the IDR13,000 level, but the amount was quite small, they said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last Thursday and Friday, was not seen in the market. \par \par \uc2  "I don't expect BI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the rupiah's weakness is due to external factors," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  Lingering concerns of further political unrest will continue to limit any upside in the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers see the rupiah trading the range of IDR12,700 to IDR13,200 for the rest of the week. \par \par \uc2  -By Kate Linebaugh; 6221 350 0145; klinebaugh@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1059GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8a06r91\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
