\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah slightly softer on weakening yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 7 (Reuters) - The rupiah was a shade softer against the dollar on Friday morning on continued weakness in the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was last given at 12,775 at 0225 GMT after opening at 12,675/12,775. The rupiah ended on Thursday at 12,650/12,750 in Jakarta and at 12,750/12,850 in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment is not as strong as in the past few days. I think it might be linked to jitters in the region on continued weakness in the yen," one American bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said resistance at the 12,500 level remained strong, suggesting a possible range of 12,600 and 12,900 for the day. \par \par \uc2  They said only a few trades had gone through so far, but operators were cautious of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions following its price checking on Thursday. Some said the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in very small amounts, indicating possible capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Chief economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita has said Indonesia would use international aid in dollars to buy rupiah in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  Ginandjar said the ecomomy's main source of trouble was a lack of international confidence reflected in the level of the rupiah compared to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  He said the government aimed to raise the rupiah to about 10,000 to the dollar by the end of March 1999. \par \par \uc2  He said that in the course of the coming months there would be continuous purchases of the rupiah in the market, which was not the same as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but should help. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market remained cautious on fears of unrest as the government has not got prices under control. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a group of 15 prominent Indonesian economists issued a declaration on Thursday warning that the country's very existence was threatened unless the government changed its economic course. \par \par \uc2  The declaration said if there was no prompt action, the situation would move towards a total destruction of the economy, bringing along the collapse of the social and political life of the people and the existence of Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  It said economic policies under President B.J. Habibie had not shown an improvement compared with the government of former president Suharto, and the government's lack of political legitimacy was impeding economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said liquidity was tighter in the morning, with overnight money for state and foreign banks hovering around 63 and 65 percent, for local banks at around 70 to 75 percent and for banks under supervision around 100 percent. \par \par \uc2  They said it might be due to carry-forward impact from a higher-than-expected allocation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weekly auction. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's due to the Wednesday effect. Many have gone short to arbitrage with the interbank market. They are now covering back," one local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The banks' weekly auction of SBIs resulted in an absorption of 14,151 billion rupiah at a weighted average interest rate of 68.33 percent, accounting for 87 percent of the incoming bids. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had targeted mopping up 13 trillion rupiah for its 28-day paper or treasury bills. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said SBIs rates were much higher than interbank rates, allowing operators to arbitrage. They said tom/next swaps eased as offshore operators unloaded their over-long positions while the longer-end was steady. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, tom/next swaps were at 15/17, one-week at 130/150, one-month at 570/620, two at 1,075/1,175, three at 1,550/1,650, six at 2,900/3,100, nine at 4,100/4,400 and one-year at 5,400/5,700 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday added rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for two more tenors in mid-morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid 51 percent for overnight money and 53 percent for four-and five-day money. The bank had earlier only set 53 percent for six-day money. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8702990\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
