\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah gains further on yen, set to test 12,500. \b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1998\par 04:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah gained further against the dollar on Wednesday morning, riding on the strengthening yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 12,670/12,770 at 0215 GMT, compared with the morning range of between 12,750 and 12,850. The rupiah ended on Tuesday at 12,950 in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah appeared to be on track to test the 12,500 resistance level. \par \par \uc2  "The momentum is there. The region seems to be in a better shape today," one American bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was nothing major expected from the monthly economics cabinet meeting on Wednesday as the July inflation and the May trade figures had been announced. \par \par \uc2  They said the yen seemed to have set a firmer tone in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the steep sell-off in U.S. stocks overnight. \par \par \uc2  "I think the U.S. economy is not immune from troubles in Asia. How do you want to sell if we can't absorb their goods. People are looking at the mark and sterling now," the American bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Deputy U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said the financial troubles in Asia might be far from over. \par \par \uc2  "I would say we have a long way to go in working through these problems," Summers told the National Governors' Association, when asked about Asia's financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  "But I think with a strong response, and particularly if the Japanese take what I think are crucial steps for them, I think this can remain very much a contained situation, and that there is no inherent reason why it needs...to pose a threat to the basic momentum of an American economic expansion." \par \par \uc2  He said the economies of South Korea and Thailand were under more control, but the situation in Indonesia was more serious. \par \par \uc2  "Relative to six months ago, I think that there is a sense of the situation coming under more control in Korea and in Thailand, relative to what most observers would have expected six months ago," Summers said. \par \par \uc2  "I think that largely for political rather than economic reasons, the situation in Indonesia is more serious than it appeared six months ago," Summers added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yield curve remained on an inverted trend, with activity in shorter-dates below one-month for arbitrage and funding purposes while the longer-end tended to soften. \par \par \uc2  One foreign bank dealer said an easing trend in the longer-term rates suggested improved rupiah expectation. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, tom/next swaps were at 15.5/16.5, one-week at 105/120, one-month at 530/570, two at 925/1,025, three at 1,400/1,475, six at 2,650/2,850, nine at 3,950/4,150 and one-year at 5,000/5,200 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said liquidity was steady, with overnight rupiah for state banks hovering around 53 percent, for banks under supervision ranging between 60 and 67 percent and for good name banks at around 60 percent. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday set rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for four tenors. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid 51 percent for overnight money, 52 percent for two-day money, 53 percent for five-and six-day money and 59 percent for seven-day money. \par \par \uc2  The bank set 13 trillion rupiah as the indicative amount for its weekly auction on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  They said the bank targetted 13 trillion rupiah for 28-day paper or treasury bills with settlement on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One local treasurer said the probability for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get 13 trillion this week was higher because operators were reluctant to place last week due to the month-end factor. \par \par \uc2  The first weekly 13 trillion rupiah auction of SBI certificates last week resulted in an absorption of 6.969 trillion rupiah at a weighted average interest rate of 65.16 percent, accounting for 91 percent of the incoming bids. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8501mdz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
