\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah holds on above the 13,000 level. \b0\par\par\uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The rupiah held on above the 13,000 level against the dollar in slow late trading on Tuesday after being driven up on a rebound in the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah ended in Jakarta at 12,950 after rising to a day's high of 12,825 from the day's low of 13,100. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volume was very thin in the afternoon, but sentiment remained positive for the rupiah to test the 12,500 level although the yen had eased from its morning high. \par \par \uc2  They said the rupiah could only keep its upward momentum if regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and especially the yen were stable. \par \par \uc2  "It's difficult for the rupiah to decouple from the region. We can just hope for the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, chief economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita said he hoped the Japanese government can stabilise the yen. \par \par \uc2  "We hope Japan can stabilise the yen. A stable yen will provide stability in the region and strengthen regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the rupiah," Ginandjar told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "I believe Japan's experienced cabinet will be able to overcome its economic problems," he said. \par \par \uc2  Ginandjar said he hoped the rupiah would also strengthen by the end of the year without giving a target figure. The IMF has said a target of 10,000 to the dollar by the end of the current fiscal year next March still appeared attainable. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said further appreciation of the rupiah towards the 12,500 and even higher levels was likely after a swathe of good news for Indonesia, ranging from some $14 billion loans to the launch of the country's first debt restructuring agency. \par \par \uc2  "The momentum is there. But you need the help of the region and further government efforts to increase domestic security, so people feel protected," one local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said swap rates were steady in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  They said the yield curve tended to be inverted following good supports in one-month swaps. \par \par \uc2  "There is a good arbitrage opportunity in one-month swaps. You can get something like 12 to 13 percent spreads," one said. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, spot/next swaps were at 15/16.5, one-week at 110/120, one-month at 550/575, two at 950/1,050, three at 1,350/1,450, six at 2,650/2,800, nine at 4,000/4,200 and one-year at 5,000/5,200 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday set rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for four tenors. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid 51 percent for overnight money, 52 percent for two-day money, 53 percent for three-and six-day money and 59 percent for seven-day money. \par \par \uc2  The bank set 13 trillion rupiah as the indicative amount for its weekly auction on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the bank targeted 13 trillion rupiah for 28-day paper or treasury bills with settlement on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One local treasurer said the probability for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get 13 trillion this week was higher because operators were reluctant to place last week due to month-end factors. \par \par \uc2  "There is also a chance rates may be higher," she said. \par \par \uc2  The first weekly 13 trillion rupiah auction of SBI certificates last week resulted in an absorption of 6.969 trillion rupiah at a weighted average interest rate of 65.16 percent, accounting for 91 percent of the incoming bids. \par \par \uc2  The average Jakarta interbank overnight interbank rates (Jibor) on Tuesday was 53.77 percent for overnight rate, 60.52 percent for one week money and 70 percent for one-month money. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8401c9m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
