\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah extends gains, rises above 13,500 on CGI. \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1998\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 29 (Reuters) - The rupiah extended its two-day gains against the dollar on Wednesday morning, breaking a strong resistance level at the 13,500 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's upward momentum continued to benefit from the on-going donors' meeting in Paris which was expected to yield another $7-$8 billion aid for Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah rose to a high of 13,400 in the morning before settling at around 13,350/13,450 at 0215 GMT. The rupiah was last traded above the 13,350 level in early June before it was pushed down to comply with Frankfurt debt restructuring scheme. \par \par \uc2  "It's the Paris meeting which seems to feed the market with optimistic sentiment," one Western bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Consultative Group for Indonesia (CGI) meeting in Paris on July 28 and 29 will decide on the amount of money pledged for the country's development projects. \par \par \uc2  Vikram Nehru, the World Bank's economist for Indonesia, said the bank was hoping donors would agree to disburse $7-$8 billion in aid to Jakarta in the year to March 1999. \par \par \uc2  World Bank officials called the meeting crucial and said the amount of money made available to Jakarta in the coming year would help determine the speed of economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was a chance for the rupiah to test the next resistance level of 13,000 if regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could maintain their stability and the yen's slide was halted. \par \par \uc2  But some said there were worries that operators could take profits once the confirmation of CGI aid came through. \par \par \uc2  Others said another factor which could weigh on the market was the new auction system with quantitative targets, allowing interest rates to be fully determined by the market. \par \par \uc2  They said operators welcomed the tender system but the worries were rates could ease before it was actually allowed to reward investors with the country's high risk profile. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see the scope for lower interest rates currently. Unlike Thailand and South Korea, Indonesia's economy has not bottomed out yet," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia on Tuesday set its first indicative target for its new auction system amounting to 13 trillion rupiah for 28-day paper, with settlement on July 30. Banks could submit bids on Wednesday between 8 a.m. and 2 p.m. (0100-0700 GMT), with the minimum bid set at 500 million rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said expectation of a possible easing in interest rates with the new quantitative target also drove short-end swaps lower, dragging other tenors to follow. \par \par \uc2  They said offshore operators were cutting down their overborrowed rupiah cash flows as local players removed their recent supports in tom/next swaps. \par \par \uc2  "People are selling now to lock in lower rates," one said. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, tom/next swaps were at 8/12, one-week at 85/105, one-month at 460/530, two at 900/980, three at 1,300/1,400, six at 2,600/2,750, nine at 4,000/4,400 and one-year at 5,200/5,600. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  set rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for three tenors, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paying 51 percent for one-day money, 59 percent for eight-day and 61 percent for 15-day. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010924du7t01b0f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
