\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah steady amid focus on riot anniversary. \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1998\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 27 (Reuters) - The rupiah was steady against the dollar on Monday morning amid plans to mark the second anniversary of riots in Jakarta following the takeover of the headquarters of the Indonesian Democratic Party (PDI) following the ousting of Megawati Sukarnoputri as party leader. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the rupiah had held on well despite fears of possible unrest connected with the anniversary. \par \par \uc2  Serious riots had followed the takeover of the PDI offices in central Jakarta in July 1996 by a government-backed faction that had deposed Megawati as PDI chief. \par \par \uc2  Ceremonies marking the occasion were being held at Megawati's home in south Jakarta after her followers had dropped a plan for a mass rally in the city centre. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was mainly traded at the 14,200 level in the morning after hovering between 14,050 and 14,300 last week. \par \par \uc2  It was quoted at 14,100/14,300 at 0240 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah was largely neglected as offshore operators focused on gloomy economic outlook in the region. \par \par \uc2  "There was not much going on in the rupiah. We see instead some pressure in the ringgit and the Singapore dollars," one Western bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said the market was waiting for the outcome of the country's donors meeting July 28 and 29 in Paris. \par \par \uc2  The Consultative Group for Indonesia (CGI) meeting would decide on the amount of loans to the country. Planning Minister Boediono said donors are likely to pledge a larger amount of loans, compared with the $5.3 billion in 1997. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a spokeswoman of the Development Cooperation ministry said on Sunday that the Dutch government had replied positively to a request of President B.J. Habibie to resume development projects to Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said liquidity was steady, with overnight money for state banks hovering between 52 and 55 percent. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday set \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for only three tenors, with the bank paying 53 percent for three-day money, 60 percent for 10-day and 61 percent for 17-day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to fine-tune its short-term monetary target in its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said swap rates were little changed, with offshores maintaining long rupiah cash flows. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, spot/next swaps were at 16/17, one-week at 110/125, one-month at 530/580, two at 1,050/1,150, three at 1,525/1,600, six at 3,000/3,200, nine at 4,400/4,800 and one-year at 5,800/6,200. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  - Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7r007py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
