\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah dives, zloty in check. \b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 6 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah continued its tumble to a six-week low in European trade on Wednesday while analysts looked to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action as the unit approached 9,000 on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Alarm at increased rioting in the northern Sumatran city of Medan wiped out earlier optimism about the country following International Monetary Fund approval of a $1.0 billion loan earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  "Unless the civil violence dies down the rupiah could go back to 10,000," said Roger Francis, senior analyst emerging markets at IBJ International. \par \par \uc2  "But I think the situation may be better than the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets suggest...People are worried that it will snowball but there's a better than even chance that it won't." \par \par \uc2  Mitul Kotecha, treasury economist at Standard Chartered, said the market was eyeing the 9,000 level in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "I think 9,000 is a key level at which you would expect some kind of resistance from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The focus is still to use monetary policy so if you would probably see rates firm up to defend the rupiah rather than any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market." \par \par \uc2  Shockwaves from \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  took their toll on other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Malaysia's ringgit a notable casualty, further weakened by comments from Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad on a possible cut in rates. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's won was also punished as stocks tumbled amid threats of an all-out strike by the Korean Confederation of Trade Unions late in May or early in June unless the government guaranteed job security. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the downside for the won appeared limited given the strong turnaround in South Korea's external position. \par \par \uc2  In Eastern Europe, the authorities struggled once again to cap a rampant zloty, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy both dollars and marks. \par \par \uc2  "The authorities don't want the zloty to appreciate too fast but I still think it is going to push higher eventually, especially after those comments yesterday by Dabrowski, though I doubt everyone on the board shares his very strong views," said Jesper Dannesboe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  Marek Dabrowski, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 10-member decision-making monetary council, said on Tuesday the zloty's crawling peg devaluation rate was too fast to reach this year's inflation target. \par \par \uc2  "Our strategy is still to buy the zloty on any dips, based on the very strong fundamentals and the fact that the council is still focusing on inflation." \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown was weaker as foreigners lightened exposure, wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following comments from Finance Minister Ivan Pilip on Tuesday that the current level of the unit did not reflect the economic situation. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the Kenyan shilling weakened further, hit by continued offshore demand for dollars. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT The following is a snapshot of emerging markets \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. ASIA\tab   * Indonesian rupiah\tab   8,900 per dollar bid vs 8,050 late in London on Tuesday. * Malaysian ringgit\tab   3.790 per dollar bid vs 3.680. Thai baht      at 38.70 per dollar vs 38.55. Philippine peso\tab   39.45 per dollar vs 39.20. * South Korean won\tab   at 1,366 per dollar vs 1,345. * Singapore dollar\tab   1.602 per dollar versus 1.583. Indian rupee\tab   39.767 per dollar vs 39.73. EUROPE\tab \tab  * Russian rouble\tab   at 6.1275 per dollar bid vs 6.11 on Tuesday. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  daily bid/offer rates 6.1080/6.1640 vs 6.1090/6.1610. * Zloty 8.27 percent above its target basket parity vs 8.437/8.347. percent at opening. Mark/Czech crown\tab      at 18.362 bid compared with 18.268. Slovak crown\tab      19.319 on mark vs 19.261. * Hungarian forint \tab 118.07 vs mark against 118.01. * Ukrainian hryvnia\tab   at 2.0467 per dollar vs 2.047. Romanian leu\tab   at 8,430 per dollar vs 8,375. AFRICA\tab \tab  & MIDEAST\tab    * Israeli shekel 3.6873 bid on dollar from Tuesday's 3.6917.\par * South African rand\tab   at 5.0535 per dollar vs 5.0575. Kenyan shilling\tab   at 61.8 vs 60.8 LATIN AMERICA\tab \tab * Mexican peso \tab  at 8.48 per dollar vs 8.473. Brazil's real\tab   at 1.1444 per dollar vs 1.1445.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London newsroom +44 171 542 6414, fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5605uom\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
